  "unverified_gaps": [
    "The human approval prompt is answered by a scripted callback registered through Hermes terminal_tool.set_approval_callback; the real approval gate, hook and registry run, but no person clicked a TUI or chat card in this run.",
    "The model-driven webhook run (S1) depends on a shared LLM pool that rate-limits gpt-6-astra; the run fell back to gpt-6.1-sol when the primary was limited (see the gateway log lines in evidence/logs).",
    "S4 to S6 use scripted proposals (not model written) on hko.e2e copies of orders_etl, with the forwarder paused for those scenarios, so the model cannot race the scripted proposal. S1 to S3 use the model proposal on hko.demo.orders_etl.",
    "S6 simulates the interruption by killing the apply process at the replay call (fault injected by the test driver into KestraClient.replay); a power loss or SIGKILL at other points is not exercised.",
    "Concurrent apply (S8) uses two processes on one machine sharing one SQLite store; separate hosts with separate stores would not share the lock.",
    "Hermes v0.23.0 was not used for the live run (validate and doctor on v0.23.0 are recorded by agent glue).",
    "Kestra OSS with basic auth only; EE namespaces, RBAC and API tokens are untested."
